Chapter: Record Cycle

  cites Codex chapter General

  cites Codex chapter Text



 Probe: ToString must not StackOverflow on deeply-nested reference

 graphs. The emitted ToString uses

 RuntimeHelpers.TryEnsureSufficientExecutionStack as a recursion

 guard so the stack doesnt run out before the traversal does.



 build-chain is tail-recursive, so constructing a 10000-deep Chain

 does not itself blow the stack. The test is the subsequent show

 traversal, which would otherwise recurse 10000 ToString frames

 deep.



Section: Types

  Chain =

    | Cons (Integer) (Chain)

    | Nil



Section: Build

  build-chain : Integer, Chain -> Chain

  build-chain (n) (acc) =

    if n <= 0 then acc

    else build-chain (n - 1) (Cons n acc)



Section: Entry Point

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act

    let root = build-chain 10000 Nil in

      print-line-uni (if text-length (show root) > 0 then "ok" else "empty")

  end



